# Probe run outputs. Generated by scripts/assess.mts against live third-party
# servers: large, machine-written, and re-derivable from a run. They are also
# written incrementally DURING a run, so a commit mid-run captures a partial
# file that is stale the moment it lands. The reproducibility envelope is the
# seed plus the rubric version, not the checked-in bytes.
assessment*.json
transcripts/

# Underscore-prefixed scripts are throwaway diagnostics — an agent or a person
# working something out at the console. They were committed once, removed a few
# hours later, and once auto-committed out from under an agent that was still
# using them. Anything worth keeping gets a real name and a comment explaining
# what question it answers.
packages/*/scripts/_*.mts
